# action-release Project

Reusable GitHub Action for automated releases. TypeScript → `dist/index.js` via @vercel/ncc.

## Required Reading

- `CLAUDE.md` — comprehensive project instructions
- `AGENTS.md` — agent quick reference
- `action.yml` — all inputs and outputs
- `README.md` — user-facing documentation with examples

## Key Resources

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `src/types.ts` | All shared types and constants |
| `src/inputs.ts` | Action input parsing and validation |
| `src/index.ts` | Entry point — orchestrates all modules |
| `action.yml` | Action metadata (inputs, outputs, branding) |

## Architecture

```
src/
├── index.ts             # Entry point
├── types.ts             # Shared types, constants, string unions
├── inputs.ts            # Parse @actions/core inputs
├── version.ts           # Version resolution (auto, package.json, file, manual)
├── bump.ts              # Keyword detection, conventional commit parsing
├── tags.ts              # Tag generation (full, all, full-and-minor)
├── previous-release.ts  # Previous release/tag detection
├── release.ts           # GitHub Release creation via API
├── template.ts          # Mustache-style template rendering
├── changelog.ts         # Conventional changelog generation
├── changelog-file.ts    # CHANGELOG.md file update
├── codename.ts          # Codename generation (7 themes)
├── llm.ts               # LLM release notes (OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter)
├── notifications.ts     # Slack, Discord, Teams, generic webhook
├── assets.ts            # File glob and upload
├── summary.ts           # GitHub Step Summary
└── __tests__/           # Vitest unit tests
```

## Verification

Before submitting: `npm run typecheck && npm test && npm run build`.
